 {"id":"MEM-POP","title":"S2 memory population — a 30-cycle run writes >=1 world/map/* and >=1 world/object/*, and the NEXT cycle retrieves one","status":"in_progress","priority":"P1","complexity":4,"depends_on":["MEM-API"],"blocks":null,"primary_model":null,"primary_provider":null,"fallback_model":null,"fallback_provider":null,"reasoning":"STAGE S2 of SPEC_agentic_memory_loop.md. ACCEPTANCE (verbatim from the spec): \"a 30-cycle run writes >=1 `world/map/*` and >=1 `world/object/*`; the NEXT cycle retrieves one\". This is the stage that attacks the spec's headline measurement: map_topology is 1,219 of 1,352 escalations (90%), because the agent cannot remember 'I have been in this room; the exit is south' and re-derives the same world fact every episode while spending a teacher call on it each time. Writes must carry the full per-write field set (key, domain, attributes, typed facts, embedding_text, confidence, evidence with run id/cycle/map/tile, applies_when where conditional) and must use the label taxonomy's world/map/<map_id> and world/object/<map_id>/<x>_<y> forms, so the run has to emit labelled facts, not a summary blob. ORDERED DIRECTLY AFTER S1 because population is only provable once the retrieval API exists - the second half of the criterion ('the NEXT cycle retrieves one') is a read-back test, so shipping writes before reads would leave the stage unverifiable.","created_at":"2026-09-26 00:45:46","worker_status":"dispatched","dispatched_at":"2026-09-26 15:49:06","worktree":"/home/kara/worktrees/ai-plays-poke-MEM-POP","branch":"wt/MEM-POP","foreman_note":"T251 wave leg 1/2: dispatched gpt-5.6-sol@openai-codex in worktree (branch wt/MEM-POP, base ae22280). Gitreins task started. Wave ai-plays-poke-2026-09-26-20-37-46."}
